{
  "id": "RADAR-2026-0006",
  "category": "compromised-package",
  "title": "Mini Shai-Hulud publishes 84 malicious @tanstack versions and spreads to MCP packages",
  "summary": "Between 19:20 and 19:26 UTC on 11 May 2026 an attacker published 84 malicious versions across 42 @tanstack packages, reaching the publish pipeline through a pull_request_target Pwn Request, GitHub Actions cache poisoning across the fork trust boundary, and extraction of an OIDC token from the runner process memory. The payload, router_init.js, harvested npm, GitHub, Vault, Kubernetes and AWS credentials, and the worm propagated to more than 200 further packages including the MCP servers @squawk/mcp and nextmove-mcp.",
